From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Verm <183540171+vermingov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:54:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] feat(linux): web-process plugin as the extension
 channel

WebKitGTK has no extension runtime, and upstream keeps its isolated-world
message handler out of product builds: WebKit rebuilds a message in the
browser process before Rust can bound it, and extension code can call the
raw handler directly.

This plugin is loaded into web processes from the context's
web-extensions directory, which WebKit mounts read-only into the sandbox.
It owns one isolated world per enabled extension, injects that extension's
content scripts there, and gives the world (and the main world of
chrome-extension://<id>/ pages) one read-only native function. The function
takes a string and a reply callback, measures the string inside the web
process and sends only messages within the limit to the browser, tagged
with the extension of the world the plugin created. No script message
handler exists.

examples/channel_probe checks each of those claims in a sandboxed
WebKitGTK view.
